---
import AppLayout from '../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Topbar from '../../../components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import AppRail from '../../../components/AppRail.astro';
import Chapter from '../../../components/Chapter.astro';
import ChapterShots from '../../../components/ChapterShots.astro';
import PrevNextApp from '../../../components/PrevNextApp.astro';
import { getApp } from '../../../data/apps';
const app = getApp('inklings-journal');
---
<AppLayout app={app}>
  <Topbar variant="app" />
  <div class="app-page">
    <AppRail app={app} current="oversikt" />
    <div class="app-flow">
      <Chapter num="01" label="Why" title={`A quiet room for <em>today's thought</em>.`}>
        <p class="lede">Inklings is built around a single idea. A diary should be small and quiet. A still room for today's thought, not a service to keep alive.</p>
        <p>There's no record to keep, no streak to lose, no reminders nagging. Skip four days, and Inklings is just as glad to see you on the fifth.</p>
        <p class="muted">Daily prompt or blank page. Local first. iCloud only if you choose.</p>
      </Chapter>
      <Chapter num="02" label="How it feels" title={`Write first. <em>The rest</em> can wait.`}>
        <p>You have ten minutes between meetings. You open Inklings, see today's prompt («What did I notice?»), write two sentences. You close it again. It didn't feel like work.</p>
        <p>The design is deliberately editorial. Newsreader serif, brass accent, drop caps. It looks more like a notebook than an app. Dark, warm background. No flashing elements.</p>
        <ChapterShots count={6} />
        <p class="muted">Face ID if you want. Markdown export when you want to take the content with you.</p>
      </Chapter>
      <Chapter num="03" label="What it does" title={`Daily prompt. <em>Search.</em> Export.`}>
        <p><strong>Daily prompt or blank page.</strong> Inklings can show a sentence to start the pen, or you can switch it off and just write.</p>
        <p><strong>Time machine and search.</strong> Flip back to this date last year. Search by word or theme across all entries. Tag system for finding your way back.</p>
        <p><strong>Local first.</strong> Everything stored in SwiftData on your device. iCloud sync is optional and opt-in. Export to markdown anytime.</p>
        <p><strong>App Intents and Siri Shortcuts.</strong> «Hey Siri, open today's Inklings» from your wrist. Small thing, but it's the kind of thing this app is built for.</p>
      </Chapter>
      <PrevNextApp slug={app.slug} />
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer label={`${app.name} · Haug & Datter`} />
</AppLayout>
